  "reason": "The current best is config_039 (multimodal, multiprofile, SCVI_n200, ViT-L, transformer, weighted) at 0.7250 accuracy. The strongest evidence shows SCVI_n200 is the best RNA encoder, ViT-L is the best image encoder, multiprofile + transformer aggregation is optimal for RNA, and weighted fusion marginally beats concat. The only untested variant keeping all best components is config_037, which swaps transformer for avgpool aggregation while retaining SCVI_n200, ViT-L, multiprofile, and weighted fusion. In RNA-only, transformer edged out avgpool (0.6530 vs 0.6501), but the multimodal setting may interact differently with the image stream. As the final experiment, this isolates the aggregation choice in the full multimodal pipeline—either confirming transformer's importance or revealing that avgpool is competitive—making it the highest-value exploitation test with the best chance of matching or exceeding the current best."
}

